  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quality Services for Health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Ghana):  The Quality Services for Health activity will provide technical assistance to the Ministry of Health and its agencies to plan and implement health system strengthening activities to build self-sustaining local systems. Using FY 2021 funds, this activity will support sustainable, quality, patient-centered services through an integrated, cross cutting approach and will particularly target maternal and child health, family planning and reproductive health, nutrition and infection prevention and control with WASH Quality Improvement (QI) to improve critical health outcomes. It will support the adoption of behaviors at the policy, management, and service provider levels to ensure quality health services. The activity will support relevant coordination mechanisms across Ministry of Health agencies to implement quality improvement initiatives and create strong linkages with regulatory bodies to enhance the regulatory environment within the national quality improvement framework. Further, the activity will support the Government of Ghana to strengthen leadership and governance of quality management structures and processes; improve institutional effectiveness of regulatory agencies to ensure quality service delivery; and improve monitoring, evaluation, and learning for continuous health system strengthening. The activity will utilize capacity building; institutional strengthening, process establishment and improvement; and enabling environment approaches to ensure country ownership and sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
